a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. legal aid;
d. repatriation and social reintegration;
e. social rehabilitation;
f. medicolegal;
g. psychological services; and
h. assistance services.
(2) Services as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus and/or related institutions based on minimum service standards established by the government.
(3) In carrying out the duties and functions of services as referred to in paragraph (1), Regional Apparatus may cooperate with related institutions and/or the community.

CHAPTER VII
COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 23
(1) The community participates in the implementation of Protection for female victims and Children involved in acts of violence.
(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in the form of:
a. establishing family partners at the neighborhood unit/community unit or sub-district/village level by the community;
b. establishing a Women and Child Protection unit/section within community organizations;
c. conducting independent socialization of the rights of Women and Children;
d. providing first aid to victims; and
e. reporting to Regional Apparatus or relevant authorized institutions if acts of violence occur in their environment.

Article 20
(1) The provision of services to victims as referred to in Article 19 is carried out every day with the principles of:
a. fast;
b. safe and comfortable;
c. empathy;
d. non-discrimination;
e. easily accessible;
f. not subject to fees; and
g. guaranteed confidentiality.
(2) The organizer or manager of services is carried out without collecting any fees from victims of violence.

